9-qms-elements", "artifact_type": "regulatory", "relevance_note": "Highlights requirements for post-market surveillance, incident handling, and corrective actions within the quality management system."}, {"artifact_id": "qmsr-820.35-records", "artifact_type": "regulatory", "relevance_note": "Emphasizes the need for maintaining records of complaints and investigations."}, {"artifact_id": "ARTIFACT-TESTLOG-2026A", "artifact_type": "test_log", "relevance_note": "Provides context regarding device confidence scores, potentially relevant to the reported irregularity. Weakly supported."}], "missing_evidence": [], "rationale": "A ventricular tachycardia-adjacent irregularity was reported, but the retrospective nature of the clinician note and lack of filing prevent confirmation of recurrence. While no adverse patient outcome was recorded, the potential for a serious cardiac event warrants investigation. The incident requires review under EU MDR Article 10(9) regarding post-market surveillance and handling of incidents (mdr-art10-9-qms-elements), as well as reporting timelines per Article 87 (mdr-art87-reporting-timelines). The lack of a filed record also raises concerns about compliance with 21 CFR \u00a7 820.35 regarding complaint records (qmsr-820.35-records).", "recommendation": "CAPA_INVESTIGATE", "requires_human_review": true, "severity": 2}, "final_report_sha256": "572bc28f372b49698234c96d3943c86e7e071075150f0262aabb0a1a8ed244ad", "generation_source": "ollama_real", "invalid_proposals": 0, "is_fallback": false, "is_mock": false, "opa_actions": [], "recommendation": "CAPA_INVESTIGATE", "record_type": "terminal", "report_id": "SYN-IND-0012", "retrievals": 1, "revisions": 0, "run_id": "SYN-IND-0012_r3", "scenario_id": "SYN-IND-0012", "schema_version": "2.1.0", "severity": 2, "shacl_findings": [], "state_terminal": "terminal", "termination_reason": "advisory_complete", "timestamp_utc": "2026-08-05T01:36:00.344016Z", "total_steps": 4, "trace_id": "42d8a26a-4b22-4082-999c-a